# Files consumed by Linux tooling must keep LF whatever platform they were
# committed from. A single CR on a shebang line is enough to make bash fail with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and systemd is no more forgiving about
# its unit files -- both of which would only show up on the VPS, after a deploy.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
deploy/config.env.oracle text eol=lf
